{"school":{"dbn":"15K146","name":"The Brooklyn New School, P.S. 146","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"15","district_label":"District 15","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"PK-5","status":"open","enrollment":638,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"610 HENRY STREET, BROOKLYN, NY 11231","phone":"718-923-4750","website":"BNS146.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/72936","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"The Brooklyn New School (BNS), PS 146, was founded in 1987 by a committee of families and teachers who wanted to create a school  with a racial, ethnic and economic balance, where children engage in active learning, where children of different skill levels work together and where families are involved in their child's education. \n\nWe are committed to academic and personal success for all students. We believe that children are creators of meaning in their own lives. They are naturally thoughtful and curious, and they work to gain understanding of the world they inhabit. When the adults who care for children foster this effort, children become life-long learners.  \n\nWe are a diverse community and our instruction is experiential and hands on with a standards based curriculum that also focuses on children\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0099s individual needs. Adults model life-long learning by engaging in ongoing professional development and our governance structure assures collaboration among families, staff and administration.","start_time":"8:10 AM","end_time":"2:30 PM","languages":"Arabic;Chinese;French;Hakka;Hebrew;Polish;Portuguese;Russian;Sinhala;Spanish;Tagalog;Taiwanese","subway":"F, G to Carroll St","bus":"B57, B61, SIM2, SIM31, SIM34, SIM35, SIM4, SIM4C, SIM4X, SIM5, X37","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":null,"latitude":40.67949,"longitude":-74.001902,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"}